---
title: Vegan Dan Dan Noodles
portions: 4
category: Chinese
source: "https://www.connoisseurusveg.com/vegan-dan-dan-noodles/"
---

## Sauce

[Mix] In a #small bowl{}, whisk the @chili-oil{60 ml}, the @water{60 ml}(hot), the @sesame-paste{45 g}, the @soy-sauce{45 ml}, the @brown-sugar{12 g}, the @garlic{2}, the @sichuan-peppercorns{1 g}(ground) and the @five-spice{1 g}. ->&dan dan sauce{}

## Tofu

[Dice] Cut the @tofu{225 g} into 5 mm cubes.

[Mix] Stir the @soy-sauce{30 ml}, the @hoisin-sauce{15 g} and the @five-spice{1 g} together. ->&tofu seasoning{}

[Fry] Heat the @peanut-oil{15 ml} in a #skillet{} over medium heat. Fry the tofu until browned, ~{8 min}.

[Glaze] Drizzle over the &tofu seasoning{} and cook until the liquid evaporates, ~{1 min}.

## Noodles

[Boil] Cook the @fresh-noodles{450 g} in #boiling water{} per package directions. Add the @spinach{170 g} for the last ~{30 s}, then drain everything together.

[Assemble] Divide the &dan dan sauce{} between four bowls. Top with the noodles, the glazed tofu, the @roasted-peanuts{35 g} and the @scallions{2}.
